lparsons@exlogcorp.exlog.com (Lee Parsons) writes:
>I am interesting in getting nethack up under DOS on a 486/25.
>What do you give up moving to a PC. 

    Well, you give up sharing your already-overworked CPU with a jillion 
other happy nethackers... You also probably give up the possibility that 
a mail-daemon will ever run up to you to deliver a Scroll of Mail.

>What I dont want to do is spent a lot of time geting hack up 
>only to go back to the unix box because I have lost 1/2 the game.

    When I loaded 3.1 on my PC at home it took all of about 15 minutes.

>any config recommendations?

    Pick a 386 or better PC with 4 megs of RAM. Configure maybe half of 
your RAM as a RAMdisk and set that option in nethack.cnf. Then get yourself 
a comfy chair and a nice table for your PC, and loosen any tight or 
constrictive clothing.

    It works for me...

